meta {
  name: Generate records from a field list
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/generate
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  limit: 10
  ~offset: 0
  ~page: 
  ~pageSize: 
  ~cursor: 
  ~max: 
  ~sortBy: 
  ~sortDirection: 
  ~q: 
  ~metadata: 
  ~resultsName: 
  seed: 1
  ~locale: 
  ~messy: 
  ~format: 
  ~delay: 
  ~trickle: 
  ~status: 
  ~fail: 
  ~auth: 
  ~safe: 
  ~table: 
  ~fields: name:person.fullName,age:number.int(18,65),status:pick(active,paused,closed|70,20,10),nickname:person.firstName?blank=15
  ~count: 
  ~constraints: end>start
}

docs {
  Describe each field as `name:generatorType`, comma-separated. Every paging, sorting, filtering, format and simulation parameter works here too.

  A type may take arguments, choices and a blank rate:

  - `age:number.int(18,65)`, `price:commerce.price(5,500,2)`, `joined:date.between(2020-01-01,2025-12-31)`: arguments in parentheses, in the order `GET /generators` lists them under `parameters`.
  - `status:pick(active,paused,closed)`: one of the choices, evenly; `pick(active,paused,closed|70,20,10)` weights them, one weight per choice. Choices are text, at most 50 of up to 64 characters.
  - `nickname:person.firstName?blank=15`: `null` in about 15% of records (`15%` works too, written `15%25` in a URL).
  - `score:number.normal(70,10,0,100,1)`, `income:number.lognormal(50000,0.5)`, `wait:number.exponential(5)`, `rank:number.zipf(1000,1)`: values that bunch the way real ones do. `normal` and `lognormal` redraw a value outside `min`/`max` up to 20 times and then clamp it.
  - `age:=age(born)`, `end:=addDays(start, days)`, `full:=concat(first, ' ', last)`: a derived field, written `=` and an expression over the record's other fields (and `index`), worked out after they are made. Numbers, text, true/false, null and dates; `+ - * / %`, comparisons, `&& || !`, `a ? b : c`, and the functions `GET /generators` lists under `functions`. It cannot loop, assign or reach anything outside the record: at most 400 characters, 150 tokens, 12 deep, 100 parts and 10 derived fields. A step that cannot be worked out gives `null`. Write `+` as `%2B` in a URL.

  `constraints=end>start,total>=subtotal` (also `end after start`, `start<end`) puts pairs of fields in order by swapping them, and moves the later one on (a day for dates, one for numbers) when a strict constraint finds them equal. At most 10; they cannot name a derived field or form a loop.

  Commas inside parentheses belong to the arguments. A type that takes no arguments, a wrong count, a value out of range or a bad weight answers `422` with `error` and the `field` it is about; an unknown type answers `400`. With `safe=true`, these types come from the safe ranges: `finance.creditCardNumber`, `image.avatar`, `image.avatarGitHub`, `image.url`, `image.urlPicsumPhotos`, `internet.domainName`, `internet.domainSuffix`, `internet.email`, `internet.ip`, `internet.ipv4`, `internet.ipv6`, `internet.url`, `phone.number`; any email inside other text moves to an example domain.

  Any other parameter that names a field filters the results: `gender=female`, `province=Ontario,Quebec`, or ranges with `age[gte]=30&age[lt]=40` (`eq`, `ne`, `gt`, `gte`, `lt`, `lte`).
}
